(R/'REPORT.md').write_text('''# Namespace ownership repair: final handoff

The small source unit is ready for parent review and combined incremental integration. The immutable [frozen report](frozen-namespace-handoff-v1/REPORT.md), [patch](frozen-namespace-handoff-v1/namespace.patch), and [pins](frozen-namespace-handoff-v1/pins.json) were published before the final runtime trial finished. They remain unchanged. Later runtime evidence is in [RUNTIME-ADDENDUM.md](RUNTIME-ADDENDUM.md).

Graphics-r6 makes the legacy P00A vendor default use BuildSystemDefaultNamespace. That default and the separate system namespace both advertised the same 41 actual SYSTEM provider records. The genuine resolver aborted on heapprofd_client_api.so, the first duplicate. The repair leaves that payload and the resolver guard intact: only DefaultConfig + VendorSection + the existing IsP00aLegacyGraphics product gate omit SYSTEM advertisements from default. BuildVendorSection's system namespace remains the exact owner of all 41 records. Requirements, paths, isolation, Binder/C++ ABI, and other product/APEX/recovery configurations remain unchanged.

The patch is relative to the system/linkerconfig project and changes one implementation file plus one new focused test file. Source preimage is `2f0851395a0bbdf3c54f0f59b7d9e76894274f493e6ae73e40783905b610d34f`; postimage is `e2aa65d9382f2f0e5c7600e5312046e4236ec2b7b1e108fa5cc12bd7d911f3c8`. Patch SHA256 is `d7c6088b233ebb0d893e46816768d11798609c499a8b64337ccf98843bb4abcc`. Full exact preimages, test postimage, and the unchanged product gate are recorded in the frozen handoff.

Original 19 host tests, fixed 26 tests, and non-P00A 22 tests pass. The selected genuine Context/builders/resolver/writer, supplied the frozen full SYSTEM PB and actual bootstrap/full APEX records, reproduce the exact duplicate before the patch. Both profiles generate base and per-APEX configurations successfully afterward; default owns zero SYSTEM records and system owns 41. Duplicate and strict missing-dependency guards remain fatal. See [test receipts](evidence/host-tests.json), [non-P00A receipt](evidence/nonlegacy-tests.json), and [actual generation](evidence/actual-generation-result.json).

An exact selected ARM64 leaf closure was available and compiled in the owned prefix with retained genuine compiler/commands and hashed dependencies. The selected preexisting stripped ELF matches the actual `/apex/com.android.runtime/bin/linkerconfig`; actual SYSTEM has no `/system/bin/linkerconfig`. The isolated fixed ELF SHA256 is `cb03a693acab8781ffa9ee4ccaca3ecd4967bd985ff87db3a23af14e5357c573` (462832 bytes). [Native candidate receipts](evidence/native-candidates.json) and the final closure seal distinguish this compiled target from the host metadata driver.

The final adapted actual-image trial completed initial and post-data namespace generation, all four BoringSSL self-tests, real manager Binder/HIDL PINGs, software Keymaster4 discovery, Keystore2 registration and earlyBootEnded IPC, 39 genuine APEX activations, and the original service-owned module-hash wait under enforcing SELinux. Its 180-second wall bound ended after odsign started. The next unchanged init command waits for odsign.key.done=1; no completion was observed. The internal odsign cause is unproved. Earlier aconfig failures remain visible in the addendum.

This qualifies the namespace contract and bounded early-service progress with an explicit candidate directory overlay. It does not qualify a production signed candidate APEX, full Android, GMS, CTS, root authentication, hardware, or flashing. All three runs, failed preparation logs, COWs and fresh DATA are preserved. Parent owns source integration and the ordinary combined native/APEX build; this worker made no active AOSP source/out edit or global build. The separately integrated device10 VINTF/userdata metadata is not present in the immutable runtime base, apart from the explicitly authorized fixture vda context line.

[HANDOFF.json](HANDOFF.json) provides paths, pins and the continuation boundary. [qualification-final.json](evidence/qualification-final.json) passes 44 evidence assertions; these summarize the recorded native tests and runtime witnesses rather than adding product acceptance.
''')
(R/'RUNTIME-ADDENDUM.md').write_text('''# Bounded actual-image runtime results after frozen publication

All three fresh owned trials have reached their declared wall limits and stopped. Run3's useful boundary is successful final namespace generation after actual post-data APEX activation and the original Keystore2 module-hash wait. It then reaches odsign start. This addendum leaves frozen-namespace-handoff-v1 unchanged.

| Trial | Bound | Result |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| r1 | 90 s | Enforcing policy denied a file bind over APEX linkerconfig. The original ELF ran and reproduced the duplicate. Logs/COW/DATA retained. |
| r2 | 90 s | Explicit directory bind admitted the isolated candidate. Initial namespace generation, real Keystore2/Keymaster IPC and 39 APEX activations passed. Module-hash wait completed with under one second left. |
| r3 | 180 s | Fresh COW/DATA/entropy; second explicit bind before final perform_apex_config. Both namespace generations passed. Progress continued to odsign start; wall limit expired. |

The r3 extension was declared because genuine r2 APEX activation took 72.221 seconds, leaving insufficient time to observe the subsequent generator. It did not change any original guard, wait or readiness property. r3 ran 2026-11-07 04:08:46.154–04:11:46.168 UTC. No fourth runtime trial was started.

Actual r3 witnesses, with guest uptime:

- Both actual init stages and policy loading ran; the public observer repeatedly read `/sys/fs/selinux/enforce` as 1. Actual ro.debuggable, ro.secure and ro.adb.secure each read 1.
- Namespace configuration generated at 4.941605 s and again at 85.367478 s, with mounted APEX metadata and no duplicate-provider fatal.
- All four actual platform/vendor 32/64-bit BoringSSL self-test services exited 0. Genuine e2fsck reported clean DATA at 11.201196 s.
- Manager IPC returned real Binder and HIDL replies. Keystore2 registered its genuine service, discovered `android.hardware.keymaster@4.0::IKeymasterDevice/default` at SOFTWARE security level, completed shared-secret negotiation and earlyBootEnded IPC, and had no observed exit. The compat wrapper's logical TRUSTED_ENVIRONMENT label does not establish a physical TEE; the actual log explicitly warns that this is software Keymaster.
- apexd activated all 39 actual packages at 84.055147 s, using genuine dm-verity/EROFS mounts. Original init waits for apexd.status=activated and keystore.module_hash.sent=true completed at 84.120860 and 84.336136 s. Actual Keystore2 logged set_module_info with 39 modules. No fixture property setter supplied these witnesses.
- derive_sdk, vdc cryptfs init_user0, derive_classpath and art_boot exited 0. odsign started at 89.821070 s. The next original init command is `wait_for_prop odsign.key.done 1`; no completion or later command was observed by 180 seconds. This wait boundary is inferred from unchanged source and the last action, not a captured internal odsign failure.

Other real errors remain recorded: early platform aconfig initialization exited 5 while copying to missing `/metadata/aconfig/maps/system.package.new`; mainline_aconfigd_init exited 1 at 86.008235 s with its reason uncaptured; lmkd repeatedly exited 0 alongside memory-cgroup feature errors; uprobestats requested unsupported PERFMON capability. These are not silently repaired or asserted to cause the odsign wait.

The runtime base is the parent's regenerated root-enabled raw, 3753902080 bytes, mode 0444, admitted SHA256 `04b4d81f486ce4a17609300c3f6d2f92cecc1938ee0f0e64019a29bd8c870785`. Its device/inode/size/timestamps/mode stayed identical before and after every trial and final sealing. No new fullraw copy or hash was made. [Admission](evidence/root-enabled-admission.json) records immutable BOOT, property, package and metadata pins; all 39 APEX packages and linker/provider metadata match the prior frozen capture. Kernel Image SHA256 `95a62a8bccd3085d682a89b6c74c7afd0961cebd1e3137b256229849920b549b` and config SHA256 `c2ea1277e1574da39d1d55d31bde7bda439ab624561ad3c6a6f4730e38f57834` stayed unchanged. The pre-root-fix image/root failures remain historical evidence; the regenerated raw does not establish runtime root authentication or final product acceptance.

Each trial uses one vCPU, 1 GiB guest RAM, no NIC/USB, at most 2.5 GiB QEMU address space, fresh 512 MiB legacy ext4 DATA and a new retained seed-exec entropy input. Seeds, their hashes, DATA contents and private key material are not exported. DATA and COWs are sealed 0444. The owned prefix at final seal held 2068278062 logical bytes and 974737408 allocated bytes, below the 2 GiB + 256 MiB allowance. All compilers/preparers used owned TMPDIR and one CPU; native compilation used at most 4 GiB address space.

The exact COW deltas are [enumerated](evidence/runtime-r3-adaptations.json) and [block-audited](evidence/runtime-r3-block-audit.json). Existing changes are vendor fstab vdb/vda mappings, two added core-init directory binds, and the authorized single vendor-context line `/dev/block/vda u:object_r:userdata_block_device:s0`. BOOT fstab mappings are separately enumerated. Additions are the narrow diagnostic observer/rc and runtime-bin overlay directory. Only linkerconfig differs from the original runtime bin payload; other binaries are byte-identical and symlink targets preserved, with original metadata and actual APEX SELinux labels. All 1422 changed guest blocks in r2/r3 are accounted for as these payload/directory/inode/allocation/superblock changes; no unexpected blocks or APEX package changes were found. This directory bind is an explicit test adaptation and gives no production APEX signature/trust qualification.

Compiled SELinux policy SHA256 `887a493f69ab16e5a0c18ba67ae715bde31c01f7cb1b75e74d2b2a35e234df4e` is unchanged. Genuine checkfc accepted the one-line context addition. Live vda context was userdata_block_device; DAC was block mode 0600, UID/GID 0. sysfs RO reads were denied to shell, so no live block RO result is claimed. The observer did not substitute a block-device open. Shell lshal could not fetch Keymaster; discovery and functional use are instead evidenced by the authorized genuine Keystore2 client. Shell could not read the protected module-hash property; actual init's completed wait and service module logs are the witnesses. ro.debuggable=1 alone did not establish reliable stdio_to_kmsg output; no exclusive suppression cause is claimed. A precreated 0600 shell-owned shell_data_file public scratch report was read using read-only debugfs after QEMU halt.

Primary evidence: [r3 serial](run-runtime-r3/serial.log), [r3 public report](evidence/actual-runtime-report-r3.txt), [r2 serial](run-runtime-r2/serial.log), [r1 serial](run-runtime-r1/serial.log), [final seal](evidence/final-seal.json), and [44 checked evidence assertions](evidence/qualification-final.json). Old run1 COW/serial and frozen handoff hashes were reverified unchanged. No device/ADB/private calibration/parent-private data, unrelated processes, active source/out writes, global Ninja/Soong, lock wait, or production integration occurred.
''')
